!
! A range's total (furrow_rules.h FW1), in Trebago: one cell per row, its
! position along its line and the range lo..hi asked of it. A cell counts
! when both 1 + pos - lo and 1 + hi - pos are at least 1, that is when
! lo <= pos <= hi. The exact sum, added from the first; a partial sum past
! 64 bits is refused, never wrapped. range.kron adds from the last, so a
! sum that passes 64 bits one way only is held.
trebago range_total
  in  pos(n), lo(n), hi(n), cell(n)
  out total
  total = sum(i, max(0, min(1, 1 + pos(i) - lo(i))) * max(0, min(1, 1 + hi(i) - pos(i))) * cell(i))
end
